From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:13:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] KITKAT: P10 followup: fix SystemUI-core Kotlin compile
 errors

The P9/P10 completion sweep added the shade carrier label, drag handle,
QS header avatar/settings/clear-all wiring and the opaque status bar
default, but referenced classes without importing them and used a
StatusBarMode value that does not exist:

- NotificationsQSContainerController: import CarrierTextManager
  (com.android.keyguard), StatusBarStateController
  (com.android.systemui.plugins.statusbar), StatusBarState and
  ShadeCarrierTextController - kotlinc failed with 'unresolved
  reference' on every use
- ShadeHeaderController: import android.widget.ImageButton/ImageView
  for the settings button, clear-all button and user avatar
- StatusBarModePerDisplayRepository: the default status bar mode was
  spelled StatusBarMode.OPAQUE, which is not a member of the enum
  (unresolved reference). Use OPAQUE_DARK instead: it is the exact
  4.4 opaque-black bar (BarTransitions.MODE_OPAQUE, renamed
  MODE_OPAQUE_DARK upstream), so no new enum value is needed.

Change-Id: I6a3746b6161233725a883927fb13c90da2261466
---
 .../shade/NotificationsQSContainerController.kt    |  4 ++++
 .../systemui/shade/ShadeHeaderController.kt        |  2 ++
 .../StatusBarModePerDisplayRepository.kt           | 14 +++++++-------
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/shade/NotificationsQSContainerController.kt b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/shade/NotificationsQSContainerController.kt
